===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|rewe}}, {{m|enm|reowe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hrēow||sorrow, regret, penitence, repentance, penance}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hreuwu||pain, sadness, regret, repentance}}. Cognates include {{cog|de|reuen|t=to regret, to repent}} and {{cog|nl|berouwen|t=to regret, to repent}}.

Probably ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*krows-}}. If so, note the same sense evolution with in this case cognate {{cog|ru|круши́ть||to destroy, to shatter}}, {{cog|ru|сокруша́ться||to be distressed, to grieve (for, over)}}. Also compare {{m+|cs|truchlit}} from {{m+|sla-pro|*truxlъ}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|sorrow}} {{lb|en|archaic|or|dialectal}} [[sorrow|Sorrow]]; [[repentance]]; [[regret]].
#: {{syn|en|contrition|misery|unhappiness|Thesaurus:sadness|Thesaurus:remorse}}
#* {{RQ:Housman Shropshire Lad|poem=XIII|stanza=2|page=21|passage=When I was one-and-twenty I heard him say again, <br> "The heart out of the bosom was never given in vain; <br> 'Tis paid with sighs aplenty and sold for endless '''rue'''." <br> And I am two-and-twenty, and oh, 'tis true, 'tis true.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|or|dialectal}} [[pity|Pity]]; [[compassion]].
#: {{syn|en|ruth|sympathy|Thesaurus:compassion}}

