===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|rewen}}, {{m|enm|ruwen}}, {{m|enm|ruen}}, {{m|enm|reowen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hrēowan|t=to rue; make sorry; grieve}}, perhaps influenced by {{der|en|non|hryggja|t=to distress, grieve}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hrewwaną|t=to sadden; repent}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=rueing}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[repent]] of or [[regret]] (some past action or event); to [[wish]] that a past action or event had not taken place.
#: {{syn|en|afterthink|deprecate|regret|repent}}
#: {{coi|en|to [[rue the day|'''rue''' the day]]}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''rued''' the day I crossed paths with her.}}
#* {{RQ:Homer Chapman Odysseys|year=1857|passage=I wept to see, and '''rued''' it from my heart.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=4| passage=Thy will chose freely what it now so justly '''rues'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=w:David Theo Goldberg|title=The Threat of Race|passage=And feminization of the homeland is something to be '''rued''', while the feminized humiliation of the enemy for the sake of the fatherland is cause for commendation and celebration.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=w:Joy Fielding|title=Still Life|passage=And was the fact she was no longer losing large chunks of time something to be celebrated or something to be '''rued'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Gary Meehan|title=True Fire|passage=“If we get in a fight, you'll be '''ruing''' your lack of training.”}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Libby Brooks|title=Nicola Sturgeon rues descent into ‘toxic’ debate on topics such as equal marriage|work=The Guardian|date=2024-12-16|url=https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/dec/16/nicola-sturgeon-rues-shift-to-toxic-debate-on-topics-such-as-same-sex-marriage|issn=0261-3077|passage=Nicola Sturgeon '''rues''' descent into ‘toxic’ debate on topics such as equal marriage [title]}}
# {{senseid|en|repent}} {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To cause to [[repent]] of sin or regret some past action.
#: {{syn|en|forthink|put the fear of God into|think over}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To cause to feel [[sorrow]] or [[pity]].
#: {{syn|en|deject|depress|Thesaurus:sadden}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|intransitive}} To feel [[compassion]] or [[pity]].
#: {{syn|en|commiserate|compassionate|feel sorry for|mercify|Thesaurus:pity}}
#* '''1842''', Nicholas Ridley<!--not the famous one, a descendant of the famous one-->, ''The Life of Nicholas Ridley''<!--the famous one-->
#*: which stirred men's hearts to '''rue''' upon them
# {{lb|en|archaic|intransitive}} To feel [[sorrow]] or [[regret]].
#: {{syn|en|grieve|mourn|Thesaurus:be sad}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1833|poem=The Death of the Old Year|passage=Old year, we'll dearly '''rue''' for you.}}

